package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Layer3D
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D
use Libraries.Game.Physics.Vehicles.Vehicle
use Libraries.Game.Physics.Vehicles.Suspension

/*
Tests that a vehicle settles on its suspension at the right height. The test
vehicle, from AddVehicle, is dropped onto the ground from just above where
its wheels touch. Each wheel's spring pushes with its stiffness, times how
far it is squeezed, times the chassis's mass, as in Bullet. The four springs
hold the vehicle up when 4 * 20 * squeeze * 800 = 800 * 9.8, so each is
squeezed by 9.8 / 80 = 0.1225, from its rest length of 0.4 to 0.2775.

The chassis center is then 0.4, the wheel's radius, plus 0.2775, plus the 0.3
the wheels hang below the center, above the ground: 0.9775.

Once settled, the chassis should fall asleep and stay asleep. A sleeping
chassis is left alone by the vehicle, as in Bullet. If the vehicle kept
pushing it with the springs, every push would wake it again.

While awake, a resting chassis reads 9.8 / 60 = 0.163 upward between steps,
because the vehicle pushes it up after each step and the next step's gravity
cancels the push. The speed checks below pass because the chassis is asleep,
which sets its velocity to 0.
*/
class VehicleRestTest is PhysicsWorldTest
    on create
        SetName("World: a vehicle settles on its suspension")
    end

    action Run
        Layer3D layer = MakeWorld()
        AddGround(layer)
        Vehicle vehicle
        Item3D chassis = AddVehicle(layer, vehicle, 1.15)

        Advance(layer, 4)

        CheckNear("chassis height", chassis:GetY(), 0.9775, 0.02)
        CheckAtMost("chassis speed", Speed(chassis), 0.05)
        CheckThat("the chassis is asleep", not chassis:IsSimulated())
        CheckNear("speed in kilometers per hour", vehicle:GetSpeedKilometersPerHour(), 0, 0.001)
        CheckNear("chassis level", GetUp(chassis):GetY(), 1, 0.001)
        CheckNear("drift along x", chassis:GetX(), 0, 0.02)
        CheckNear("drift along z", chassis:GetZ(), 0, 0.02)

        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < vehicle:GetSuspensionSize()
            Suspension wheel = vehicle:Get(i)
            CheckThat("wheel " + i + " touches the ground", wheel:GetInContact())
            CheckNear("wheel " + i + " suspension length", wheel:GetSuspensionLength(), 0.2775, 0.02)
            i = i + 1
        end
    end
end
